"""
Step 1.2: High-Precision Permission Analysis Engine

Architecture Philosophy:
    "Beyond Pattern Matching - Semantic Understanding Through Program Analysis"

This engine implements a three-stage pipeline to generate structured "Permission Profiles"
for each function, capable of dissecting complex, multi-layered access control logic ranging
from simple onlyOwner checks to sophisticated RBAC and beyond.

Three-Stage Architecture:
    Stage 1: Guard Statement Identification (Scanning Phase)
             → Wide net scan to identify all potential guard statements

    Stage 2: Permission Heuristic Filtering (Brain Phase)
             → AChecker-inspired: Filter conditions that depend on BOTH
               (a) Transient Caller (from step1.1)
               (b) Authorization State (from contract state variables)

    Stage 3: Semantic Parsing & Classification (Translation Phase)
             → Translate code-level conditions into structured, human-readable format
             → Identify patterns: OWNABLE, RBAC, WHITELIST, STATE_CHECK, SIGNATURE, etc.

Output: Permission Profile - A structured JSON object detailing all permission requirements
        for each function, distinguishing true permission checks from business logic.

Author: Chief Static Analysis Architect
"""

